Also available in G to avoid the (Bm).

TIP:  For the opening strum |A| once and then, still holding the (A), pick the covered 3rd, 2nd, and 1st strings followed by single strums of the chords until you get to the second D.  This one-strum pattern repeats at the end of the chorus.

TIP:  Also in the chorus extend the chord to the back half of “wind” even though it’s one syllable.
       

